by nicolas-grekas at 2026-08-12T13:33:11Z

Thanks for your patience with how long this sat.

I rebased onto 8.2 and squashed. The five commits conflicted with the branch (`#[Argument]` and `#[Option]` gained `suggestedValues`, `#[AsCommand]` gained `listedAt`), so I reapplied the change by hand:

 * `description` on `#[Argument]` and `#[Option]`, `description` and `help` on `#[AsCommand]`, all accept `string|callable` and are resolved in the constructor, so the public properties stay plain strings and nothing downstream changes.
 * The `is_string()` check comes first, so a description that happens to name a PHP function stays a description. Pinned by a test on all three attributes.
 * CHANGELOG moved to the 8.2 section, phpdoc updated with `string|(callable():string)`.
 * Tests are two focused cases per attribute rather than threaded through the existing definition tests, and I left `Php8Command2` alone to keep the diff to the feature.

Verified: the two new callable tests fail on 8.2 with a `TypeError` and pass with the change; the Console suite is at 1862 tests with the same two pre-existing `QuestionHelperTest` failures as on the branch tip.

On the design question I raised back then, your answer holds up. The callable can only return static data, but PHP has no function calls in constant expressions, so building a description out of an enum's cases is not expressible today. And on PHP 8.5 the callable can be an inline `static function () {}` or a `self::generate(...)` reference, both of which are constant expressions there and both of which need exactly this change to be accepted, which is what @GromNaN pointed at from the start.

👍 from me.

I also rewrote the title and description. A doc PR on symfony/symfony-docs is still needed, would you open one?
